//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 300
//@ expect-stdout-contains: CIRC28_DRUG_RISPERIDONE_PASS
//
// Risperidone + 9-hydroxyrisperidone (paliperidone) on the circ28 drug record, coupled by
// circ28_metab.sio (stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_drug_risperidone.sio; parameter table and sources
// in its header). CYP2D6 extensive metaboliser (EM) unless stated.
//
// ROUND 1 TEXT BELOW IS HISTORY: in round 2 the split is fitted to the EM/PM clearance ratio and the IV ratio 3 is a validation
// row (see the ROUND 2 block further down for the current fits, predictions and results).
//
// FITTED, hence NOT validations (one observable per fitted parameter):
//   R Kp scalar -> Vss 109.5 L; R total hepatic clint -> IV CL 23.6 L/h (fe_R 0.02 sets the renal part);
//   R split clform/other -> IV AUC ratio 9-OH/risperidone = 3 (Huang 1993); R ka -> Tmax 1.0 h;
//   M Kp scalar -> Vss 136.4 L; M clint, clren -> CL 3.81 L/h and fe_M 0.59.
//   The EXTRA fit that the sources force: the IV ratio 3 with CL_M 3.81 gives phi = clform/(clform+clint)
//   0.487, i.e. 9-OH formation carries only about half of the hepatic clearance of risperidone.
//
// VALIDATIONS (none of the numbers below enters a fit), criteria fixed BEFORE the runs:
//   an observation with a between-subject SD (label CV x mean): |z| <= 2;
//   an observation with no spread: the prediction within a factor 1.5.
//
// PREDICTIONS WRITTEN BEFORE THE FIRST COUPLED RUN. CLOSED FORM (Sounio scratch evaluation of the
// fitted record, no coupled run): Eh_R 0.3471, F = fa Fg (1-Eh) = 0.6529, F_src of 9-OH 0.9777, phi 0.4865,
// CL_R,hep 23.128 + renal 0.472 L/h, PM (clform = 0) total CL_R 14.86 L/h, ka fit 0.8120 /h.
//   V1  F risperidone              0.653   obs 0.66 (Huang 1993, no spread) and 0.70 CV 25 % (label)   PASS
//   V2  oral AUC ratio 9-OH/R      4.59 = 3/F (formation is route independent: sequential first
//                                  pass, linear kinetics, no gut-wall metabolism)  obs 6 (Huang 1993)   PASS at 1.5 (fold 1.31),
//                                  an UNDER-prediction by 23 % that the fits cannot remove: 6 needs a first-pass-specific
//                                  yield (a gut-wall or CYP3A route that forms 9-OH), which one clform slot cannot carry.
//   V3  active-moiety F            (F + 3)/4 = 0.913 (plasma concentrations summed)  obs 1.00 (Huang)   PASS (fold 1.10)
//   V4  R terminal t1/2            ESTIMATE ~3.3 h (ln2 Vss/CL; range 2.5-4.5)  obs 3 h (CV 30 %, label)   PASS
//   V5  9-OH terminal t1/2         ESTIMATE ~24.8 h (ln2 Vss/CL_M, range 20-30)  obs 21 h (CV 20 %, label)  PASS (z ~0.9)
//   V6  active-moiety t1/2         ESTIMATE ~24 h  obs 20 +/- 2.5 (Huang)   BORDERLINE (z ~1.6-2); no pre-commitment
//   V7  9-OH Tmax (oral)           ESTIMATE 3-5 h  obs 3 h (label, no spread)   PASS if <= 4.5 h
//   V8  PM oral ratio 9-OH/R       0 (clform = 0: no 9-OH is formed at all)  obs 0.2 (Huang)   FAIL (a stated limit:
//                                  PMs still form 9-OH, via CYP3A4, Mahatthanatrakul 2011; not in the record)
//   V9  PM R t1/2                  5.1 h (ln2 Vss/CL_PM)  obs 22 h (Huang) and 20 h CV 40 % (label)   FAIL at 1.5 (fold 4.3)
//   The PM scaling is CYP2D6 pathway only: clform x 0 (PMs lack CYP2D6, defining the phenotype in Huang 1993).
//   It fails twice because the sources disagree with each other: IV ratio 3 (EM) with CL_M 3.81 needs phi 0.49,
//   but the PM half-life 22 h (3 h in EM) needs the CYP2D6 share of the parent clearance to be >= 0.86.
//   The fit chooses the IV ratio (an observable of its own), so the PM t1/2 pays for it.
// NOT VALIDATED (no absolute value opened): Cmax and Tmax of both after a stated oral dose in healthy EM.
//   Remmerie 2016 gave profiles in figures only, Narayanan 2026 (PMID 42053037) gave no absolute values in the
//   abstract, Kneller 2020 and Boonleang 2010 full texts are closed. Cmax is printed per mg for reference only.
//
// RESULTS (first kernel run, Madaros; the predictions above were not changed afterwards)
//   V1 0.653 pass; V1b z -0.27 pass; V2 oral ratio 4.63 vs 6 (fold 0.77) pass; V2b pass; V3 0.919 pass;
//   V4 R t1/2 3.77 h (z 0.86) pass; V5 9-OH t1/2 25.4 h (z 1.05) pass; V6 active-moiety t1/2 25.4 h vs 20 +/- 2.5
//   (z 2.2) FAIL, borderline as foreseen; V7 9-OH Tmax 9.0 h vs 3 h FAIL (fold 3.0) AGAINST the pre-registered PASS:
//   the estimate 3-5 h was wrong. Diagnosis: the 9-OH curve is formation-rate limited AND the uniform Kp scalar gives
//   it a 136 L volume that fills slowly through the 3.8 L/h clearance; the label's 3 h implies a much smaller central
//   volume than a single Kp scalar can give. Not fixable by any fit allowed here (one observable per parameter).
//   V8 PM ratio 0 vs 0.2 FAIL (by construction); V9 PM R t1/2 5.6 h vs 22 h FAIL (fold 0.26), z -1.8 vs the label's
//   wide CV 40 % (pass only because of that CV). The assertions below are bands around these measured numbers.

// =====================================================================================================
// ROUND 2 (restructured split). The round-1 split phi was fitted to the IV AUC ratio 3 (abstract level,
// from two clearances I could not open). Round 2 fits instead the CYP2D6 share f2D6 of the parent hepatic
// clearance to ONE EM/PM observable: the PM/NM ratio of dose-adjusted steady-state risperidone concentration,
// 6.20 (95 % CI 5.05-7.62), pooled over oral studies, Zhang 2020 Pharmacotherapy 40:632 (PMID 32519344, abstract
// read) -> (CL/F)_EM / (CL/F)_PM = 6.2, u 0.65 (from the log CI). The CYP2D6 pathway forms 9-OH entirely; the
// rest of the hepatic clearance (1 - f2D6) is split by q = fraction that forms 9-OH (CYP3A4 etc.).
// q has NO independent observable in the sources I could read ("lesser extent CYP3A4", no number), so the base
// case sets q = 0 (PM forms no 9-OH: the PM-ratio failure is kept, not fitted away) and S4b scans q as a
// DIAGNOSIS. The IV ratio 3, the oral ratio 6, PM ratio 0.2, PM half-life 22 h, the PM/NM active-moiety
// ratio 1.44 (Zhang 2020, 95 % CI 1.23-1.69) and the 9-OH Tmax are VALIDATION rows in round 2.
// Fitted in round 2 (so NOT validations): Vss_R, CL_R, fe_R, f2D6 (to the 6.2), Tmax_R (ka), Vss_M, CL_M, fe_M.
//
// ROUND 2 PREDICTIONS, written before any round-2 run. Hand arithmetic from the round-1 closed forms
// (CL/F_EM = 23.6/0.653 = 36.1 L/h; PM target 36.1/6.2 = 5.83 L/h; Eh_PM ~0.075; tot_PM ~53 against tot_EM 360.7):
//   f2D6 ~0.85 (0.84-0.86)         coordinator expected ~0.86
//   R1  IV ratio 9-OH/R  = MWr f (1-fe) F_src CL_R/CL_M = 1.039 x 0.853 x 0.98 x 0.9777 x 6.194 = 5.26  vs 3: fold 1.75 FAIL
//                          (coordinator: ~5.3, FAIL: agree)
//   R2  oral ratio = IV ratio / F = 5.26/0.653 = 8.06   vs 6: fold 1.34 PASS, now OVER-predicted (coordinator ~8: agree)
//   R3  F 0.653 PASS (unchanged); active-moiety F (F+5.26)/(1+5.26) = 0.945 PASS
//   R4  PM R t1/2 (kernel) ~14-16 h (ln2 Vss/CL_PM,total 0.693 x 109.5/5.4 = 14.1 h + tail)   vs 22 h (Huang): fold ~0.68 PASS;
//       vs label 20 h CV 40 %: z ~ -0.6 PASS   (coordinator: passes: agree)
//   R5  PM oral ratio 0 (q = 0)  vs 0.2: FAIL (kept on purpose)
//   R6  PM/NM active-moiety AUC: AUC_R,PM = F_PM/CL_PM = 0.925/5.4 = 0.171, M_PM = 0 -> AM_PM/AM_EM = 0.171/0.251 = 0.68  vs 1.44: FAIL
//   R7  9-OH Tmax (oral) = 9.0 h, UNCHANGED from round 1. Reason (my prediction against the coordinator's 5-7 h): total parent clearance,
//       Vss, ka and the 9-OH disposition are all unchanged, so the SHAPE of the 9-OH curve is unchanged and only its height
//       scales with f2D6; the first-pass share of 9-OH formation is Eh/(1-0) ~ 0.35 whatever f2D6 is. FAIL vs 3 h (fold 3).
//       A one-compartment bound: Tmax = ln(kf/ke)/(kf-ke) with kf = ln2/3.8 h, ke = ln2/25.4 h gives 12.4 h; the multi-compartment
//       kernel gives less (9 h) but the formation limit is what sets the scale.
//   R8  active-moiety t1/2 25.4 h unchanged: FAIL (z 2.16), as in round 1.
// =====================================================================================================

// =====================================================================================================
// ROUND "TRANSIT" (2026-11-15). Everything above is history (rounds 1-2, first-order input); round 2 numbers are the BASELINE:
// ka 0.8120 /h, R oral 1 mg Cmax 4.171 ng/mL, 9-OH Tmax 9.029 h, oral ratio 8.1045, AM AUC 251.88 ng h/mL per mg, test 3.06 s compiled.
// CHANGE: the oral input is an Erlang chain of ntr = 4 stages (n = 3 transit compartments, a DECLARED ASSUMPTION, plus 1: common
// rules 11; no risperidone-specific transit number was read); CD_KA = k per stage, refitted to the SAME observable (oral Tmax 1.0 h,
// Risperdal label); tlag 0 (none sourced); fa 1. Cmax, Cmax/AUC, MTT are validation rows, never fitted.
// GUT Kp: the whole validation is run for gv 0 (V_ss scalar on every organ, gut included) and, in a compact column, for gv 1 (gut wall at
// its Rodgers-Rowland Kp, scalar refitted with circ28_kp_scale_for_vss_gutrr, k refitted); gv 1 is adopted only if it improves the failing
// peak rows (V7) and worsens no other row beyond its uncertainty.
//
// PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTIONS (written before any run of the changed code beyond `souc check`; the only runs before this block were the
// UNCHANGED round-2 test, whose numbers are the baseline above). Outcomes go in the RESULTS block at the end of this header, never here.
//   T1  k (1/h per stage), gv 0                               3.5 - 5.5 (point 4.3; first-order ka 0.812); MTT 4/k 0.73 - 1.15 h
//   T2  R oral 1 mg Tmax = 1.0 h by the fit; R Cmax          4.7 - 6.0 ng/mL per mg (point 5.2; baseline 4.171): the chain is more
//       peaked than the first-order input at the same Tmax, Cmax rises by 12 - 45 %
//   T3  9-OH Tmax (oral, EM)                                 8.7 - 9.1 h (point 8.9; baseline 9.029): the input change moves it by
//       less than 0.4 h and the row V7 (label 3 h) stays FAIL, fold 2.9 - 3.0: the delay is formation-limited (parent t1/2 3.8 h),
//       not input-limited. The IV-route 9-OH Tmax (9.990 h) is unchanged to 1e-3 (no oral input)
//   T4  AUC rows unchanged (linear kinetics, closed forms do not contain the input): F 0.6529, IV ratio 5.254, oral ratio 8.1045,
//       active-moiety AUC 251.88, f2D6 0.85, to 0.3 %; V1, V1b, V2, V2b, V3 keep PASS; VI keeps FAIL
//   T5  terminal half-lives unchanged: R 3.773 h, 9-OH 25.41 h (+/- 0.3 %); V4, V5 PASS, V6 FAIL
//   T6  PM rows (V8-V10) keep their verdicts (FAIL, PASS for V9b, FAIL, FAIL); PM R Tmax 1.5 - 1.9 h (baseline 1.912, no observation)
//   T7  gut Kp: R scalar within 3 % of gv 0; every peak row changes by less than 2 % between gv 0 and gv 1 and the AUC rows by less
//       than 0.5 %; gv 1 is NOT adopted (no failing row improves by more than 2 %; 9-OH Tmax is formation-limited)
//   T8  mass balance of the chain input <= 1e-9 (R and 9-OH); input given equals the dose to 1e-9
//   T9  budget: AM AUC relative u 0.10 - 0.13 (0.115); CL_M obs share of var(AM AUC) 70 - 80 % (76 %); Tmax_R share 0 (AUC does not
//       see the input)
//   T10 compiled run time 2.5 - 4.5 s (baseline 3.06 s); no validation row changes its verdict
//
// RESULTS (recorded after the runs, 2026-11-15; Madaros, the default engine and lean_single print the marker):
//   T1  HIT   k 5.1335 /h per stage (gv 1: 4.8935; round 2 first-order ka 0.8120), MTT 0.779 h, mode of the input rate 0.585 h
//   T2  MISS  R oral 1 mg Cmax 7.046 ng/mL (predicted 4.7-6.0; round 2 4.171): +69 % at the same Tmax 1.0 h, Cmax/AUCinf 0.255 /h (0.151)
//   T3  MISS  9-OH Tmax 8.406 h (predicted 8.7-9.1; round 2 9.029): the input change moves it by -0.62 h, more than the 0.4 h foreseen;
//             V7 fold 2.80 (predicted 2.9-3.0), verdict FAIL kept. IV-route 9-OH Tmax 9.990 h unchanged (hit). The delay stays
//             formation-limited: input MTT 0.78 h against the parent t1/2 3.77 h and the 9-OH t1/2 25.4 h
//   T4  HIT   F 0.6529, IV ratio 5.254, oral ratio 8.1045, AM AUC 251.88 ng h/mL per mg unchanged (the budget AM AUC is identical to 6 digits)
//   T5  HIT   R t1/2 3.7733 h, 9-OH t1/2 25.406 h; V4, V5 PASS, V6 FAIL
//   T6  HALF  verdicts hit (V8 FAIL, V9 FAIL, V9b PASS, V10 FAIL); MISS PM R oral Tmax 1.139 h (predicted 1.5-1.9; round 2 1.912)
//   T7  HIT   R scalar gv 1 1.6057 against gv 0 1.5874 (+1.2 %); peak rows move by at most 1.1 % (R Cmax), 9-OH Tmax by 0.4 %, AUC rows
//             by 0; R t1/2 by 0.6 % (not pre-registered); gv 1 NOT adopted
//   T8  HIT   input given = dose to 1e-9, mass balances R and 9-OH <= 1e-9 (oral and IV)
//   T9  HIT   AM AUC relative u 0.1150, CL_M obs share 76.1 %, Tmax_R share 0 (AUC does not see the input). NEW rows, not pre-registered:
//             R Cmax relative u 0.32 (CL_R obs 62 %, Tmax_R 33 %), 9-OH Tmax u 2.94 h (CL_R obs 84 %, Tmax_R 0.9 %)
//   T10 HIT   compiled run 2.9-3.2 s user (round 2: 2.7-3.0 s); no validation row changes its verdict
//   Verdict changes against round 2: none (V7 FAIL kept at fold 2.80, was 3.01).
//   The rows marked [MISS] in the body are the pre-registered ranges that missed; each is paired with a regression band on the measured value.
// COMPILER WORKAROUNDS ADDED IN THIS ROUND: the gv 1 records are built in `main`, before the first section, and the gv 1 column is computed
// by rt_gcol into a [f64; 16] before the sections that hold the big arrays (scratch programs of this work: a main with four records and
// several [f64; 18] values segfaulted at run time on Madaros, as did a fit called from a callee frame).
// =====================================================================================================

use darwin_pbpk::circ28::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_kp::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_metab::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug_risperidone::*
use math::pure::{ln}

fn rt_fold(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, fold: f64, expect_pass: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let r = pred / obs
    var ok: i32 = 0
    if r <= fold && r >= 1.0 / fold { ok = 1 }
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  pred "); print(pred); print("  obs "); print(obs); print("  fold "); print(r)
    if ok == 1 { println("  [pass]") } else { println("  [fail]") }
    if ok != expect_pass {
        println("  [FAIL] outcome differs from the pre-registered one")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

fn rt_z(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, sd: f64, expect_pass: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let z = (pred - obs) / sd
    var ok: i32 = 0
    if z <= 2.0 && z >= 0.0 - 2.0 { ok = 1 }
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  pred "); print(pred); print("  obs "); print(obs); print("  SD "); print(sd); print("  z "); print(z)
    if ok == 1 { println("  [pass]") } else { println("  [fail]") }
    if ok != expect_pass {
        println("  [FAIL] outcome differs from the pre-registered one")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

fn rt_band(tag: string, v: f64, lo: f64, hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    if v >= lo && v <= hi { return 0 }
    print("  [FAIL] "); print(tag); print(" = "); print(v); print(" outside ["); print(lo); print(", "); print(hi); println("]")
    return 1
}

// A pre-registered range: prints HIT or MISS and never fails; a miss is paired with a regression band on the measured value.
fn rt_pre(tag: string, v: f64, lo: f64, hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    if v >= lo && v <= hi {
        print("  [HIT]  "); print(tag); print(" = "); println(v)
    } else {
        print("  [MISS] "); print(tag); print(" = "); print(v); print(" outside the pre-registered ["); print(lo); print(", "); print(hi); println("]")
    }
    return 0
}

fn rt_rel(tag: string, got: f64, want: f64, tol: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var d = got - want
    if d < 0.0 { d = 0.0 - d }
    d = d / want
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  got "); print(got); print("  want "); print(want); print("  rel "); println(d)
    if d > tol {
        println("  [FAIL] above tolerance")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

// One coupled run. mode 0 = EM; mode 1 = PM: the CYP2D6 formation is removed and the non-2D6 hepatic clearance
// (the record's clint, valid because the base q is 0) is re-split with q forming 9-OH; mode 2 = DIAGNOSTIC only,
// parent hepatic clearance x3 (clint and clform).
fn rt_run(dr: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug, route: i32, dose: f64, mode: i32, q: f64, res: &![f64; 24]) with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var thr = circ28_drug_theta(dr)
    if mode == 1 {
        let rest = thr[CD_CLINT]
        thr[CD_CLFORM] = q * rest
        thr[CD_CLINT] = (1.0 - q) * rest
    }
    if mode == 2 {
        thr[CD_CLFORM] = 3.0 * thr[CD_CLFORM]
        thr[CD_CLINT] = 3.0 * thr[CD_CLINT]
    }
    let thm = circ28_drug_theta(dm)
    rsp_run_th(thr, thm, route, dose, 0.1, 12.0, 36.0, 120.0, 240.0, res)
}

// CL/F of risperidone from the record (mode 0) or its PM version with q = 0 (mode 1), closed form.
fn rt_clf(dr: &Circ28Drug, mode: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th = circ28_drug_theta(dr)
    if mode == 1 {
        th[CD_CLFORM] = 0.0
    }
    let p = circ28_drug_params_theta(th)
    let eh = circ28_hepatic_extraction(p)
    return (eh * circ28_q_hepatic(p) * p.bp + th[CD_CLREN]) / (1.0 - eh)
}

fn rt_show(tag: string, r: &[f64; 24]) with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    print(tag); print(": R Cmax "); print((*r)[0]); print(" Tmax "); print((*r)[1]); print(" AUCinf "); print((*r)[2]); print(" t1/2 "); println((*r)[3])
    print("      M Cmax "); print((*r)[5]); print(" Tmax "); print((*r)[6]); print(" AUCinf "); print((*r)[7]); print(" t1/2 "); println((*r)[8])
    print("      balance R "); print((*r)[10]); print(" M "); print((*r)[11]); print(" fits ok R/M "); print((*r)[13]); print("/"); println((*r)[14])
}

fn rt_pk(dr: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return rsp_f_oral(circ28_drug_theta(dr))
}

fn rt_budget(dr: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let b = rsp_budget(dr, dm, 1.0)
    print("S5 uncertainty budget with refit, 1 mg oral: "); print(b.runs); println(" coupled runs")
    fails = fails + rt_band("AM AUC (ng h/mL per mg)", b.am_auc * 1000.0, 240.0, 265.0)
    fails = fails + rt_band("AM AUC relative u", sqrt_f(b.var_am) / b.am_auc, 0.09, 0.14)
    print("  active-moiety AUC "); print(b.am_auc * 1000.0); print(" ng h/mL per mg  u "); print(1000.0 * sqrt_f(b.var_am)); print("  rel "); println(sqrt_f(b.var_am) / b.am_auc)
    print("  risperidone AUC "); print(b.r_auc * 1000.0); print("  u "); println(1000.0 * sqrt_f(b.var_r))
    print("  9-OH AUC "); print(b.m_auc * 1000.0); print("  u "); println(1000.0 * sqrt_f(b.var_m))
    print("  oral ratio "); print(b.ratio); print("  u "); print(sqrt_f(b.var_ratio)); print("  vs 6: z "); println((b.ratio - 6.0) / sqrt_f(b.var_ratio))
    println("  input          u(input)      share of var(active-moiety AUC) %")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 16 {
        print("  "); print(rsp_input_name(i)); print("   "); print(b.u[i]); print("   "); println(100.0 * b.contrib_am[i] / b.var_am)
        i = i + 1
    }
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T9 AM AUC relative u (0.10-0.13)", sqrt_f(b.var_am) / b.am_auc, 0.10, 0.13)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T9 CL_M obs share of var(AM AUC) % (70-80)", 100.0 * b.contrib_am[13] / b.var_am, 70.0, 80.0)
    fails = fails + rt_band("T9 Tmax_R share of var(AM AUC) % (AUC does not see the input)", 100.0 * b.contrib_am[12] / b.var_am, 0.0, 1.0e-6)
    println("  NEW in this round (not pre-registered): R Cmax and 9-OH Tmax enter the budget; the Tmax_R input now carries the input")
    print("  R Cmax (ng/mL per mg) "); print(1000.0 * b.rcmax); print("  u "); print(1000.0 * sqrt_f(b.var_rcmax)); print("  rel "); println(sqrt_f(b.var_rcmax) / b.rcmax)
    print("  9-OH Tmax (h) "); print(b.mtmax); print("  u "); print(sqrt_f(b.var_mtmax)); print("  rel "); println(sqrt_f(b.var_mtmax) / b.mtmax)
    println("  input          share of var(R Cmax) %    share of var(9-OH Tmax) %")
    var jb: i32 = 0
    while jb < 16 {
        print("  "); print(rsp_input_name(jb)); print("   "); print(100.0 * b.contrib_rcmax[jb] / b.var_rcmax); print("   "); println(100.0 * b.contrib_mtmax[jb] / b.var_mtmax)
        jb = jb + 1
    }
    fails = fails + rt_band("R Cmax relative u (regression band)", sqrt_f(b.var_rcmax) / b.rcmax, 0.0, 1.0)
    return fails
}

fn sqrt_f(x: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !(x > 0.0) { return 0.0 }
    var g = x
    if g < 1.0 { g = 1.0 }
    var k: i32 = 0
    while k < 60 {
        g = 0.5 * (g + x / g)
        k = k + 1
    }
    return g
}

// 9-OH alone, IV 1 mg over 0.1 h: does the metabolite's own distribution delay a peak? (diagnostic)
fn rt_malone(dm: &Circ28Drug) with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let th = circ28_drug_theta(dm)
    let r = circ28_run_theta(th, circ28_dose_iv(1.0, 0.1, 0.05, 3.0, 0.5, 240.0, 120.0, 240.0))
    print("  9-OH given alone IV 1 mg over 0.1 h: Tmax "); print(r.tmax); print(" h, t1/2 "); print(r.thalf); print(" h, AUCinf "); println(r.auc_inf)
}

// ---- gut-wall Kp column (gv 1: gut wall at its Rodgers-Rowland Kp; V_ss scalars of R and 9-OH refitted with circ28_kp_scale_for_vss_gutrr;
// k refitted to the same oral Tmax 1.0 h, rsp_ka_fit_g(1)). g[]: 0 oral R Cmax, 1 oral R Tmax, 2 oral M Cmax, 3 oral M Tmax, 4 oral R AUC,
// 5 oral M AUC, 6 oral R t1/2, 7 oral M t1/2, 8 IV R AUC, 9 IV M AUC, 10 PM R Cmax, 11 PM R Tmax, 12 R scalar, 13 M scalar, 14 V_ss R, 15 V_ss M
fn rt_g_oral(thr: [f64; 18], thm: [f64; 18], g: &![f64; 16]) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var res: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rsp_run_th_g(thr, thm, 1, 1.0, 0.1, 12.0, 36.0, 120.0, 240.0, 1, &!res)
    (*g)[0] = res[0]
    (*g)[1] = res[1]
    (*g)[2] = res[5]
    (*g)[3] = res[6]
    (*g)[4] = res[2]
    (*g)[5] = res[7]
    (*g)[6] = res[3]
    (*g)[7] = res[8]
}

fn rt_g_iv(thr: [f64; 18], thm: [f64; 18], g: &![f64; 16]) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var res: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rsp_run_th_g(thr, thm, 0, 1.0, 0.1, 12.0, 36.0, 120.0, 240.0, 1, &!res)
    (*g)[8] = res[2]
    (*g)[9] = res[7]
}

fn rt_g_pm(thr_in: [f64; 18], thm: [f64; 18], g: &![f64; 16]) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var thr = thr_in
    thr[CD_CLFORM] = 0.0
    var res: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rsp_run_th_g(thr, thm, 1, 1.0, 0.1, 12.0, 36.0, 120.0, 240.0, 1, &!res)
    (*g)[10] = res[0]
    (*g)[11] = res[1]
}

fn rt_gcol(dr1: &Circ28Drug, dm1: &Circ28Drug, g: &![f64; 16]) with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let thr = circ28_drug_theta(dr1)
    let thm = circ28_drug_theta(dm1)
    rt_g_oral(thr, thm, g)
    rt_g_iv(thr, thm, g)
    rt_g_pm(thr, thm, g)
    (*g)[12] = thr[CD_KPSC]
    (*g)[13] = thm[CD_KPSC]
    let pr = rsp_params(thr, 1)
    let pm = rsp_params(thm, 1)
    (*g)[14] = circ28_vss_plasma(pr)
    (*g)[15] = circ28_vss_plasma(pm)
}

fn rt_grow(tag: string, v0: f64, v1: f64, lo: f64, hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  gv0 "); print(v0); print("  gv1 "); print(v1); print("  gv1/gv0 "); println(v1 / v0)
    return rt_band(tag, v1 / v0, lo, hi)
}

fn rt_gut(sc0: f64, g: &[f64; 16], po: &[f64; 24], iv: &[f64; 24], pmr: &[f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S6 gut-wall Kp: column gv 1 (gut wall at its Rodgers-Rowland Kp; V_ss scalars refitted; k refitted to the same Tmax) against gv 0")
    print("  Kp scalar R: gv0 "); print(sc0); print("  gv1 "); print((*g)[12]); print("   9-OH gv1 "); println((*g)[13])
    print("  k per stage: gv0 "); print(rsp_ka_fit_g(0)); print("  gv1 "); print(rsp_ka_fit_g(1)); println(" /h")
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T7 R scalar gv1 within 3 % of gv0", (*g)[12] / sc0, 0.97, 1.03)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("V_ss R of the gv 1 record (L)", (*g)[14], rsp_obs_r_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("V_ss 9-OH of the gv 1 record (L)", (*g)[15], rsp_obs_m_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("gv 1 oral R Tmax = 1.0 h (refit check)", (*g)[1], rsp_obs_r_tmax(), 2.0e-4)
    println("  validation rows, gv 0 | gv 1 | ratio (peak rows must move by less than 2 %, AUC rows by less than 0.5 %)")
    fails = fails + rt_grow("IV AUC R (ng h/mL per mg)       ", 1000.0 * (*iv)[2], 1000.0 * (*g)[8], 0.999, 1.001)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("IV AUC 9-OH (ng h/mL per mg)    ", 1000.0 * (*iv)[7], 1000.0 * (*g)[9], 0.999, 1.001)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral AUC R (ng h/mL per mg)     ", 1000.0 * (*po)[2], 1000.0 * (*g)[4], 0.995, 1.005)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral AUC 9-OH (ng h/mL per mg)  ", 1000.0 * (*po)[7], 1000.0 * (*g)[5], 0.995, 1.005)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral R Cmax (ng/mL per mg)      ", 1000.0 * (*po)[0], 1000.0 * (*g)[0], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral 9-OH Cmax (ng/mL per mg)   ", 1000.0 * (*po)[5], 1000.0 * (*g)[2], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral 9-OH Tmax, V7 (h)          ", (*po)[6], (*g)[3], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral R t1/2 (h)                 ", (*po)[3], (*g)[6], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("oral 9-OH t1/2 (h)              ", (*po)[8], (*g)[7], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("PM R Cmax (ng/mL per mg)        ", 1000.0 * (*pmr)[0], 1000.0 * (*g)[10], 0.98, 1.02)
    fails = fails + rt_grow("PM R Tmax (h)                   ", (*pmr)[1], (*g)[11], 0.98, 1.02)
    print("  failing row V7: 9-OH Tmax fold over 3 h "); print((*po)[6] / 3.0); print(" -> "); println((*g)[3] / 3.0)
    println("  DECISION: gv 1 is NOT adopted. The one failing peak row (V7, 9-OH Tmax) improves by 0.4 % (2.802 -> 2.791 fold), far below the 2 %")
    println("  that would justify it, and no AUC row moves (closed forms do not contain Kp). The 9-OH delay is formation-limited (S4c), not a gut-Kp effect;")
    println("  gv 0 stays the module's variant.")
    return fails
}

fn main() with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var dm = circ28_drug_new()
    var dr = circ28_drug_new()
    // the steps of rsp_drug_into, written out in main: lean_single mis-forwards the second reference when
    // they are chained inside one function (measured: it gave clint 178.0 / clform 182.6 instead of 185.2 / 175.5)
    rsp_measured_m(&!dm)
    rsp_fit_record_m(&!dm)
    rsp_measured_r(&!dr)
    rsp_fit_record_r(&!dr)
    rsp_ka_record(&!dr)
    var dm1 = circ28_drug_new()
    var dr1 = circ28_drug_new()
    rsp_measured_m(&!dm1)
    rsp_fit_record_m_g(&!dm1, 1)
    rsp_measured_r(&!dr1)
    rsp_fit_record_r_g(&!dr1, 1)
    rsp_ka_record_g(&!dr1, 1)
    var g1: [f64; 16] = [0.0; 16]
    rt_gcol(&dr1, &dm1, &!g1)
    println("S0 record: R then 9-OH (value, status)")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        print("  R "); print(i); print(" "); print(circ28_drug_value(&dr, i)); print("  status "); print(dr.status[i])
        print("   |  M "); print(circ28_drug_value(&dm, i)); print("  status "); println(dm.status[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    // ---- S1: the fits reproduce their own observables
    println("S1 the fits reproduce their observables (NOT validations)")
    let pr = circ28_drug_params(&dr)
    let pm = circ28_drug_params(&dm)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("V_ss R (L)", circ28_vss_plasma(pr), rsp_obs_r_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("V_ss M (L)", circ28_vss_plasma(pm), rsp_obs_m_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("CL R total (L/h)", circ28_splanchnic_clearance(pr) * pr.bp + circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLREN), rsp_obs_r_cl(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("CL M total (L/h)", circ28_splanchnic_clearance(pm) * pm.bp + circ28_drug_value(&dm, CD_CLREN), rsp_obs_m_cl(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("(CL/F)_EM/(CL/F)_PM (closed form) = 6.20 [fitted]", rt_clf(&dr, 0) / rt_clf(&dr, 1), rsp_obs_pmratio(), 1.0e-6)
    print("  f2D6 = clform/(clform+clint) = "); println(circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLFORM) / (circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLFORM) + circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLINT)))
    // ---- S2: IV run (the IV ratio 3 is now a VALIDATION row)
    var iv: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rt_run(&dr, &dm, 0, 1.0, 0, 0.0, &!iv)
    rt_show("S2 IV 1 mg over 0.1 h", &iv)
    fails = fails + rt_band("IV balance R", iv[10], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_band("IV balance M", iv[11], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    // ---- S3: oral EM
    var po: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rt_run(&dr, &dm, 1, 1.0, 0, 0.0, &!po)
    rt_show("S3 oral 1 mg EM", &po)
    println("V validation, predicted vs observed (criteria fixed before the runs; round-2 predictions in the header)")
    let f_cf = rt_pk(&dr)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("VI  IV AUC ratio 9-OH/R, Huang 3         ", iv[7] / iv[2], 3.0, 1.5, 0)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V1  F risperidone (closed form)         ", f_cf, 0.66, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_z("V1b F risperidone vs label 0.70 CV 25 % ", f_cf, 0.70, 0.175, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V2  oral AUC ratio 9-OH/R, Huang 6       ", po[7] / po[2], 6.0, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V2b oral ratio / IV ratio = 1/F         ", (po[7] / po[2]) / (iv[7] / iv[2]), 1.0 / f_cf, 1.1, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V3  active-moiety F (oral/IV AUC)       ", (po[2] + po[7]) / (iv[2] + iv[7]), 1.0, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_z("V4  R t1/2 (h), label 3 h CV 30 %       ", po[3], 3.0, 0.9, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_z("V5  9-OH t1/2 (h), label 21 h CV 20 %   ", po[8], 21.0, 4.2, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_z("V6  active-moiety t1/2 (h), Huang 20 +/- 2.5", po[8], 20.0, 2.5, 0)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V7  9-OH Tmax (h), label 3 h             ", po[6], 3.0, 1.5, 0)
    // round-2 bands around the measured outcomes
    fails = fails + rt_band("IV ratio band (hand prediction 5.26)", iv[7] / iv[2], 5.0, 5.5)
    fails = fails + rt_band("oral ratio band (hand prediction 8.06)", po[7] / po[2], 7.8, 8.4)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T3 9-OH Tmax (h), oral EM (8.7-9.1)", po[6], 8.7, 9.1)
    fails = fails + rt_band("9-OH Tmax, measured regression band (round 2 first-order input: 9.029 h)", po[6], 8.35, 8.46)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T3 V7 fold 9-OH Tmax over label 3 h (2.9-3.0)", po[6] / 3.0, 2.9, 3.0)
    fails = fails + rt_band("f2D6 band (hand 0.85)", circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLFORM) / (circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLFORM) + circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_CLINT)), 0.84, 0.86)
    // ---- round "transit": the input rows (pre-registered T1, T2, T4, T5, T8; each miss paired with a regression band)
    println("S3t oral input, 4-stage chain (3 transit compartments assumed): k per stage, MTT, mode, Cmax, mass balance")
    let kfit = rsp_ka_fit()
    print("  k "); print(kfit); print(" /h (round 2 first-order ka 0.8120), MTT ntr/k "); print(circ28_transit_mtt(kfit, rsp_ntr())); print(" h, mode of the input rate (ntr-1)/k "); print(circ28_transit_mode(kfit, rsp_ntr(), 0.0)); println(" h")
    fails = fails + rt_rel("record CD_KA = k of rsp_ka_fit", circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_KA), kfit, 1.0e-12)
    fails = fails + rt_rel("oral Tmax of R = 1.0 h (the fitted observable, grid 0.05 h)", po[1], rsp_obs_r_tmax(), 2.0e-4)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T1 k per stage (3.5-5.5)", kfit, 3.5, 5.5)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T1 MTT (0.73-1.15 h)", circ28_transit_mtt(kfit, rsp_ntr()), 0.73, 1.15)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T2 R oral 1 mg Cmax (4.7-6.0 ng/mL)", 1000.0 * po[0], 4.7, 6.0)
    fails = fails + rt_band("R oral Cmax, measured regression band (round 2: 4.171 ng/mL)", 1000.0 * po[0], 6.95, 7.15)
    print("  R Cmax / AUCinf (1/h) "); print(po[0] / po[2]); print("  round 2 first-order 0.1508")
    println("")
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T5 R terminal t1/2 unchanged (3.773 +/- 0.3 %)", po[3], 3.762, 3.784)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T5 9-OH terminal t1/2 unchanged (25.41 +/- 0.3 %)", po[8], 25.33, 25.48)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T4 oral ratio unchanged (8.1045 +/- 0.3 %)", po[7] / po[2], 8.080, 8.129)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T4 AM AUC unchanged (251.88 +/- 0.3 ng h/mL)", 1000.0 * (po[2] + po[7]), 251.1, 252.6)
    fails = fails + rt_band("T8 input given equals the dose (mg)", po[9], 0.999999999, 1.000000001)
    fails = fails + rt_band("T8 mass balance R, oral", po[10], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + rt_band("T8 mass balance M, oral", po[11], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    // ---- S4: poor metaboliser (CYP2D6 formation removed; q = 0)
    var pmr: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rt_run(&dr, &dm, 1, 1.0, 1, 0.0, &!pmr)
    rt_show("S4 oral 1 mg PM (clform_2D6 removed, q = 0)", &pmr)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V8  PM oral ratio 9-OH/R, Huang 0.2     ", pmr[7] / pmr[2] + 1.0e-12, 0.2, 1.5, 0)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V9  PM R t1/2 (h), Huang 22 h            ", pmr[3], 22.0, 1.5, 0)
    // round-2 prediction R4 said 14-16 h, fold ~0.68, PASS: measured 14.55 h, fold 0.661 < 1/1.5: FAIL by 1 %. My miss.
    fails = fails + rt_z("V9b PM R t1/2 vs label 20 h CV 40 %     ", pmr[3], 20.0, 8.0, 1)
    fails = fails + rt_fold("V10 PM/NM active-moiety AUC, Zhang 1.44  ", (pmr[2] + pmr[7]) / (po[2] + po[7]), 1.44, 1.5, 0)
    fails = fails + rt_band("PM R t1/2 band (hand 14-16)", pmr[3], 14.0, 15.2)
    fails = fails + rt_band("PM/NM AM band (hand 0.68)", (pmr[2] + pmr[7]) / (po[2] + po[7]), 0.65, 0.71)
    fails = fails + rt_pre("T6 PM R oral Tmax (1.5-1.9 h; round 2 1.912, no observation)", pmr[1], 1.5, 1.9)
    fails = fails + rt_band("PM R Tmax, measured regression band", pmr[1], 1.12, 1.16)
    // S4b DIAGNOSIS (not validation): fraction q of the non-2D6 hepatic clearance that forms 9-OH in PMs.
    println("S4b diagnosis: PM with q = fraction of the non-2D6 hepatic clearance forming 9-OH (what do 0.2 and 1.44 need?)")
    var jq: i32 = 0
    while jq < 5 {
        var qv: f64 = 0.0
        if jq == 1 { qv = 0.1 }
        if jq == 2 { qv = 0.25 }
        if jq == 3 { qv = 0.5 }
        if jq == 4 { qv = 1.0 }
        var rr: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
        rt_run(&dr, &dm, 1, 1.0, 1, qv, &!rr)
        print("  q "); print(qv); print("  ratio "); print(rr[7] / rr[2]); print("  AM PM/NM "); print((rr[2] + rr[7]) / (po[2] + po[7]))
        print("  R t1/2 "); print(rr[3]); print("  M Tmax "); print(rr[6]); print("  M t1/2 "); println(rr[8])
        jq = jq + 1
    }
    // S4c DIAGNOSIS of the 9-OH Tmax (formation-rate limited or distribution of the metabolite?)
    println("S4c diagnosis of the 9-OH Tmax (not a fit)")
    print("  M Tmax: IV R "); print(iv[6]); print(" h, oral R "); print(po[6]); println(" h")
    var fast: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    rt_run(&dr, &dm, 1, 1.0, 2, 0.0, &!fast)
    print("  parent hepatic clearance x3 (diagnostic): R t1/2 "); print(fast[3]); print("  M Tmax "); println(fast[6])
    let kf = 0.6931471805599453 / po[3]
    let ke = 0.6931471805599453 / po[8]
    print("  one-compartment M fed at the parent rate: Tmax = ln(kf/ke)/(kf-ke) = "); println(ln(kf / ke) / (kf - ke))
    rt_malone(&dm)
    fails = fails + rt_gut(circ28_drug_value(&dr, CD_KPSC), &g1, &po, &iv, &pmr)
    // ---- S5: budget
    fails = fails + rt_budget(&dr, &dm)
    if fails == 0 { println("CIRC28_DRUG_RISPERIDONE_PASS") } else { print("FAILS "); println(fails) }
}
